# Password hashing (docs/design/33-crypto.md, "Passwords"): Argon2id PHC
# strings with a fresh salt each time, verification, the unusable hash, and
# a malformed hash, which matches nothing instead of panicking. Parameters
# are the OWASP minimum for Argon2id: m=19456 (19 MiB), t=2, p=1.

### a hash verifies its password and no other, and is salted
POST /pw.PasswordProtocol/RoundTrip
content-type: application/json
connect-protocol-version: 1

{"password": "correct horse battery staple", "other": "correct horse battery stapler"}
>>> 200
json {"value": "same=true wrong=false salted=true phc=true"}

### an empty password hashes and verifies too
POST /pw.PasswordProtocol/RoundTrip
content-type: application/json
connect-protocol-version: 1

{"password": "", "other": " "}
>>> 200
json {"value": "same=true wrong=false salted=true phc=true"}

### no password matches the unusable hash
POST /pw.PasswordProtocol/Unusable
content-type: application/json
connect-protocol-version: 1

{"password": ""}
>>> 200
json {"value": false}

### a malformed hash matches nothing
POST /pw.PasswordProtocol/Against
content-type: application/json
connect-protocol-version: 1

{"password": "x", "hash": "not a hash"}
>>> 200
json {"value": false}
